# SCHLAR — PROMPT 8: RECEPTIONIST / FRONT OFFICE WORKSPACE
## Complete Implementation | Professional UI | User-Friendly Workflows | Integrated Demo Functionality

You are continuing development of **SCHLAR**, an existing school-management web and mobile frontend project.

Implement Prompt 8: the **Receptionist / Front Office workspace**.

This is an extension of the existing application, not a new application. Prompts 1–7 have already established the foundation and multiple role workspaces. Inspect the current project, understand its implementation, and build this workspace using the existing architecture.

The goal is to create a professional, efficient, intuitive front-office system that helps school reception staff manage visitors, enquiries, appointments, calls, incoming requests, student-related front-office services, and daily reception operations.

The workspace must be genuinely interactive. Forms must validate, buttons must perform their stated actions, records must update, search and filters must work, and relevant dashboard statistics must reflect the underlying demo data.

**Core SCHLAR principle: “Simple enough for a first-time user, powerful enough for a real school.”**

Simplify navigation and workflows without removing important capabilities, records, permissions, or operational controls.

